description.narrative:
1) Capacity for business management, trade, and access to finance and technology by women and smallholder farmers increased;
2) Production of high-value crops, especially those produced by women and smallholder farmers, and promoted through access to new international markets increased;
3) Specific technical support to overcome bureaucratic barriers to export and established country trade;
 4) Lowering domestic barriers to agricultural exports through adoption of dispute resolution mechanisms and expansion of e-governance services: Foreign Trade Portal Created and Functional; Enhancement of the National Arbitration Centre (NAC) to resolve legal and commercial disputes, mitigate contract enforcement risks and improve the country's business environment. Access to legal information and legal advisory services to women-owned agribusiness SMEs facilitated.
